<title>BELGIUM: EU announces merger probe in grocery sector.</title>
<headline>EU announces merger probe in grocery sector.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it was opening a routine probe into the following corporate venture under the European Union's merger rules, which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions:</p>
<p>-- Plans by British supermarket group Tesco Plc to buy Ireland's biggest grocery chain from Associated British Foods (ABF) for 630 million pounds. (Notified on April 1.) Tesco will take control of 75 Quinnsworth and Crazy Prices stores in Ireland as well as 34 stores in Northern Ireland trading as Stewarts, Crazy Prices, Superdeal, Westside Stores and Bloomfield, plus a processing business, an off-licence chain and a sports shop group.</p>
<p>The Commission has about a month to approve the deal or start a full probe.</p>
